The general form of vla_in_loop's rule, and only the IR backend has it. C99
6.2.4p6 ends a VLA's lifetime with the block that declared it; step 19 puts the
stack pointer back on every edge leaving such a block, so the storage is reused
by the next allocation and this fixture reads that off the addresses.

The legacy backend gives none of it back before the function returns - the same
design that keeps it out of vla_in_loop, its temporaries being addressed from
rsp rather than from the frame pointer - and is not going to be taught to. So
this is skipped there rather than muted: there is no bug here waiting to be
fixed and flagged.
